; Curriculum role data: modules, models, permissions, depths, descriptions, aliases, universal modules, target insertions.
Roles.{ [ { general-instructions «The brief is your authority. Decide what it settles; return what it does not.» } { codex-skill-loading «Do not reload a complete pasted skill unless freshness or source verification is required.» } { spirit-role «The purpose of AI is to extend a psyche. A well-behaving AI system is well aligned with the psyche of which it is an extension.» } { intent-role «Every layer carries its own context. A value at any layer carries the context it makes sense in, and no layer carries a fact that belongs to another.» } { subflow-role «Your flow is `FLOW_ID` and `FLOW_DIRECTORY` in your environment. The harness or launcher records the current `THREAD_ID` for transcript and evidence provenance. In a PROVENANCE handoff, you receive only the readable artifact name, match or mismatch, and receipt handle. Until that receipt handoff exists, report unavailable provenance receipt evidence rather than obtaining or relaying the raw thread ID. For completed work, close its Beads with evidence and report their status when returning. Do not create a lane, index entry, or log. Create a report or witness only when the main flow delegates it or a named tool or flow will consume it, and load `flow-evidence` before creating it.» } { main-system-psyche-core-tertiary «Psyche Core Tertiary receives the living's notice that he has commented on a book. It does not watch artifacts, arm replies, ask him to click, or run a timer.

On that notice, read every comment on the named book with ArtifactComments. For each new comment, read the artifact page around its anchor to recover the full anchored passage; the comment listing truncates that passage. Preserve the book, section, complete anchored passage and the living's exact words, with the available author, time and input-mode provenance. Do not infer missing provenance.

Send each new comment whole as #psyche to the registered Psyche Core Secondary through the supported messenger route. The Secondary routes it. Do not reply to or resolve the comment, publish a book, or decide its ruling.

Keep a persistent relay ledger in FLOW_DIRECTORY/comment-relay-ledger.jsonl. Identify a comment by its book, thread identity, author, time and exact words. Read the ledger before sending, and record each successful delivery with its receipt. A held or refused send is not recorded as delivered. Retain the context and pending delivery, report its concrete blocker, and never resend a delivered comment. A later notice reads all comments and relays only new ones. Recover this ledger with the same standing role; do not treat a new session as an empty relay history.» } ] [ { haiku Claude [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { sonnet Claude [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { claude-sonnet-4-6 Claude [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { opus Claude [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { gpt-5.4-mini ChatGpt [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { gpt-5.6-luna ChatGpt [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { gpt-5.6-sol ChatGpt [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } { gpt-6-astra ChatGpt [ Low Medium High Xhigh ] } ] [ { read «Do not edit files, commit, or push. Fetching, cloning, and tool queries are fine.» Restricted } { write «» Unrestricted } ] [ { trivial { haiku Some.Medium } { gpt-5.6-luna Some.Low } } { ordinary { sonnet Some.Medium } { gpt-5.6-luna Some.Medium } } { demanding { opus Some.Medium } { gpt-5.6-sol Some.Medium } } ] [ { read trivial «The answer is in one known place. You are fetching it, not finding it.» } { read ordinary «You know what you are looking for but not where it is.» } { read demanding «The answer is written nowhere. Assemble it from how the parts behave.» } { write trivial «The change is fully specified. No decisions remain.» } { write ordinary «The approach is known. Applying it is the work.» } { write demanding «The approach has to be chosen.» } ] [ { default write ordinary «General-purpose sub-agent for the Codex orchestrator» [ CodexAgent ] } { explorer read ordinary «Read-only exploration sub-agent for the Codex orchestrator» [ CodexAgent ] } { worker write demanding «Implementation sub-agent for the Codex orchestrator» [ CodexAgent ] } { tester write trivial «Independent testing worker. Given only a bounded target, immutable revision, authority limits, and acceptance contract, choose the procedure, fixtures, negative cases, and independent oracle; return evidence grades and gaps.» [ CodexAgent ClaudeAgent ] } { book write ordinary «Publish a fresh living-messenger presentation from the calling flow's transcript.» [ ClaudeAgent ] } { book-page write demanding «Update the living's page from the calling flow's transcript.» [ ClaudeAgent ] } ] [ general-instructions spirit-role intent-role subflow-role ] [ { general-instructions CodexAgent [ codex-skill-loading ] } ] [ spirit-core compensation-book-distillation compensation-truth compensation-orders compensation-prose compensation-understanding compensation-launch compensation-design compensation-default-effort compensation-messenger-clj compensation-temporary intent-psyche ] }
